{"id": "EUVD-2026-48613", "enisaUuid": "4400324b-d350-3b2a-9e75-1a5cc9492bca", "description": "Datasets through 5.0.0, fixed in commit f989ef9, contains a path traversal vulnerability in folder-based dataset builders where the file_name metadata field is not properly validated before being joined to the dataset directory. Attackers can supply crafted file_name values with directory traversal sequences to read arbitrary local files, which are then embedded into output when save_to_disk or push_to_hub is called.", "datePublished": "2026-07-24T14:58:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-01T15:20:14", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:A/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/huggingface/datasets/issues/8324", "https://github.com/huggingface/datasets/pull/8325", "https://github.com/huggingface/datasets/commit/f989ef9b4cc6c0039a7a82458eebca49e2b58b4b", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/datasets-path-traversal-via-unsanitized-file-name-metadata"], "aliases": ["PYSEC-2026-3716", "CVE-2026-66007", "GHSA-379c-qx7v-6h59"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.55, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3b10ce9a-4b96-3e2c-b511-0b52eafd1df1", "product": {"name": "datasets", "vendor": {"name": "huggingface"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22645.0.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "564f81f7-85c2-3ae8-9e18-b3c3b5279946", "vendor": {"name": "huggingface"}}], "isExploited": false}